# AGENTS.md: Working agreement

This repo is built to be handed between agents (and humans). Follow this and a
fresh agent can pick up any unit of work without prior context. If a rule here
conflicts with a request, surface the conflict rather than silently overriding it.

## The loop (every session)

1. Read STATUS.md → find the current phase and the notes for the next agent.
2. Pick one unit of work whose dependencies are done. Read its plan/phase doc fully.
3. Work on a branch (`feat/<short-slug>` or `phase-N/<short-slug>`).
4. Record any non-trivial decision as a new ADR in `docs/adr/`.
5. Update STATUS.md **in the same PR**: what was done, what was deferred, what the
   next session should pick up.

## Non-negotiables (Definition of Done)

Copy-pasteable into a PR description; the PR template mirrors this list.

- [ ] Lint, typecheck, and tests are green locally.
- [ ] New behavior has tests; every bug fix has a regression test that fails
      against the broken code.
- [ ] STATUS.md updated in this PR.
- [ ] Any non-trivial decision recorded as an ADR.
- [ ] No secrets, no committed data, no `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}`-external paths.

