## ADR discipline

Non-trivial decisions get `docs/adr/NNNN-kebab-title.md` from the template. Keep
ADRs short (aim for a page). Never delete or edit an accepted ADR — supersede it
and link both ways.

## Commits & branches

- Conventional Commits: `feat(scope):`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `ci:`.
  Subject ≤ 72 chars, imperative; body explains *why* (the diff shows what).
- One unit of work per PR where possible. Delete branches after merge.

## Code conventions

- Strict typing everywhere. No escape hatches (`any`, `# type: ignore`) without a
  `// why:` comment — the comment, not the linter, is the gate.
- Validate all external data at the boundary (schema-parse payloads, not trust).
- Prefer leaving a clear seam + a TODO referencing the plan doc over guessing.

## When you're unsure

Record the question as an open decision in STATUS.md and stop. Do not imply
something exists when it is unbuilt.
